1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,488
Today is October 23, 2026.

3
00:00:07,488 --> 00:00:15,135
Overnight, Wall Street absorbed a sharp divergence across benchmark assets as liquidity crosscurrents rattled equity markets.

4
00:00:15,135 --> 00:00:23,334
The Nasdaq plunged six hundred ninety-four points, dropping two point six percent and breaching its one-hundred-twenty-day moving average.

5
00:00:23,334 --> 00:00:30,589
The S and P five hundred fell ninety-three points to seventy-six sixty-three, defending seventy-six twenty support.

6
00:00:30,589 --> 00:00:38,763
Meanwhile, the Dow Jones Industrial Average bucked the trend, rising eleven points to post its third consecutive positive session.

7
00:00:38,763 --> 00:00:46,300
Sector rotation into defensive utilities, healthcare, and staples accelerated as capital abandoned high-beta tech.

8
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:54,731
Ten-year Treasury yields eased slightly from five point three percent to five point fifteen percent, remaining near multi-decade highs.

9
00:00:54,731 --> 00:01:01,728
These elevated long rates continue to restrict private sector borrowing and do the Federal Reserve's tightening work for them.

10
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:09,032
With the November elections approaching, interest rate futures price an eighty-five percent chance of a Fed pause next week.

11
00:01:09,032 --> 00:01:13,260
However, December rate hike odds sit near ninety percent.

12
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:21,324
Adding fuel to the inflation debate, Brent crude surged past one hundred twelve dollars per barrel amid escalating Middle East friction.

13
00:01:21,324 --> 00:01:26,839
In response, Washington released emergency fuel reserves to cap price spikes.

14
00:01:26,839 --> 00:01:34,474
The CNN Fear and Greed Index collapsed to twenty, signaling extreme fear, while the VIX jumped fourteen percent.

15
00:01:34,474 --> 00:01:41,054
This macro liquidity squeeze is directly colliding with artificial intelligence capital expenditure cycles.

16
00:01:41,054 --> 00:01:45,025
The market is now brutally punishing negative cash flows.

17
00:01:45,025 --> 00:01:51,741
Meta shattered investor sentiment after third-quarter capital expenditures reached nearly thirty-five billion dollars.

18
00:01:51,741 --> 00:01:57,758
That pushed free cash flow into negative territory at minus two point one billion dollars.

19
00:01:57,758 --> 00:02:06,447
In response, Meta announced a one-to-one Class C non-voting stock dividend to enable equity financing without diluting founder voting control.

20
00:02:06,447 --> 00:02:10,858
Five-year credit default swaps on Meta surged to record highs.

21
00:02:10,858 --> 00:02:16,888
Yet physical AI demand signals tell a contrasting story of relentless real-world adoption.

22
00:02:16,888 --> 00:02:24,645
South Korean semiconductor exports surged two hundred twenty-two percent through mid-October, led by unyielding chip demand.

23
00:02:24,645 --> 00:02:31,410
Multi-layer ceramic capacitor lead times at Samsung Electro-Mechanics stretched to a full fifty-two weeks.

24
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:39,425
Super Micro Computer raised its revenue guidance to nineteen billion dollars, refuting rumors of an enterprise hardware slowdown.

25
00:02:39,425 --> 00:02:43,481
Let us now turn to our key individual equities for today.

26
00:02:43,481 --> 00:02:45,736
First, Nvidia.

27
00:02:45,736 --> 00:02:51,177
NVDA remains the premier valuation anchor across mega-cap semiconductors.

28
00:02:51,177 --> 00:03:00,442
Unlike competitors trading at lofty multiples, Nvidia maintains the lowest valuation among the Magnificent Seven alongside top-tier profitability.

29
00:03:00,442 --> 00:03:10,920
At the Berlin industrial conference, Nvidia showcased its expansion from datacenters into full-stack industrial AI, factory digital twins, and autonomous mobility.

30
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:15,380
Technically, primary entries sit near two hundred eight dollars.

31
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:23,248
Heavy secondary support rests below two hundred dollars, backed by its two-hundred-fifty-day moving average at one hundred ninety-nine.

32
00:03:23,248 --> 00:03:25,417
Second, Tesla.

33
00:03:25,417 --> 00:03:33,616
TSLA delivered forty-eight-point-six-five thousand vehicles with free cash flow beating expectations at one point five billion dollars.

34
00:03:33,616 --> 00:03:39,179
Management revealed one point seven four million paid Full Self-Driving subscribers.

35
00:03:39,179 --> 00:03:47,341
However, operating profit dropped fifty-six percent, and full-year capital expenditure guidance was trimmed to twenty billion dollars.

36
00:03:47,341 --> 00:03:52,684
Investors are grappling with whether this signals capital discipline or slowing innovation.

37
00:03:52,684 --> 00:04:01,790
Meanwhile, market speculation swirls around a three-point-seven trillion dollar merger structure with SpaceX, though regulatory obstacles remain steep.

38
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:07,697
Tesla key support zones stand firm at three hundred fifty-two and three hundred forty dollars.

39
00:04:07,832 --> 00:04:10,147
Third, SpaceX.

40
00:04:10,097 --> 00:04:17,548
SPCX achieved its first profitable quarter in company history, booking fourteen point six billion dollars in revenue.

41
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:26,077
Its enterprise AI compute division surged eight hundred thirty percent, generating over seven point five billion dollars to surpass Starlink.

42
00:04:26,077 --> 00:04:32,045
Morgan Stanley and JPMorgan raised target prices aggressively toward five hundred dollars.

43
00:04:32,045 --> 00:04:38,969
The initial public offering price of one hundred thirty-five dollars serves as an unbreakable institutional cost floor.

44
00:04:38,969 --> 00:04:41,334
Finally, Alphabet.

45
00:04:41,334 --> 00:04:49,815
GOOG has slipped below its two-hundred-fifty-day moving average, now trading under Berkshire Hathaway's three-hundred-seven-dollar cost basis.

46
00:04:49,815 --> 00:04:57,879
Concerns over escalating AI infrastructure outlays and delayed commercial agent rollouts weigh heavily ahead of next week's earnings.

47
00:04:57,879 --> 00:05:04,876
With hedge fund short positioning reaching five-year peaks, the setup for a violent short squeeze grows by the day.

48
00:05:04,876 --> 00:05:11,298
Maintain strict risk parameters, respect technical baselines, and protect cash reserves.

49
00:05:11,298 --> 00:05:15,305
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

50
00:05:15,305 --> 00:05:19,472
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
